   "text": "I read the structure in pieces and joined them into one SMILES. The wedge/hash assignments at the spiro carbon are the least certain part of the reading.\n\n**Fragments**\n- **Isoindolinone\u2013glutarimide end:** a 3-(1-oxoisoindolin-2-yl)piperidine-2,6-dione. The alkyne sits at C4 of the isoindolinone, on the benzene carbon next to the CH2.\n- **Linker:** the alkyne runs to C5 of an imidazole. Its N1 carries a three-carbon chain (CH2CH2CH2) to an amide NH.\n- **Benzamide:** that amide is a para-disubstituted benzene. The other substituent is an anilide NH that is acylated by the pyrrolidine carboxamide.\n- **Spiro core:** the pyrrolidine runs N\u2013C2\u2013C3\u2013C4\u2013C5.\n  - C2 carries the carboxamide (hashed bond).\n  - C3 carries the 3-chloro-2-fluorophenyl group (wedge).\n  - C4 is the spiro carbon of a 6-chloro-oxindole. I read the bond to the oxindole aromatic carbon as hashed and the bond to the oxindole C=O as a wedge.\n  - C5 is the spiro carbon of the cyclohexane. It has two identical ring arms, so it gets no stereo label.\n- **Aryl substituent:** attached carbon, then C\u2013F (ortho), then C\u2013Cl (meta), then three CH.\n\n**Stereo**\nI worked out each centre from the 2D coordinates and the wedge/hash bonds:\n- C2: `[C@@H]`\n- C3: `[C@H]`\n- C4 (spiro oxindole): `[C@]`\n\nSMILES: O=C(Nc1ccc(cc1)C(=O)NCCCn1cncc1C#Cc1cccc2c1CN(C1CCC(=O)NC1=O)C2=O)[C@@H]1NC2(CCCCC2)[C@]3(c4ccc(Cl)cc4NC3=O)[C@H]1c1cccc(Cl)c1F"
